+# Wide-screen web Play entries — isolated candidate
+
+This is a UI/admission overlay against the supplied CardStashy 4.0.5 fixture. It was not pushed, deployed, or activated, and does not certify engine or release readiness.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Desktop header and bottom-nav Play nodes stay exactly where they are; `index.html` is unchanged. Existing desktop eligibility remains independent of window size. Desktop touch hybrids retain desktop placement.
+- Known mobile/tablet web devices with reported touch input receive a rounded glass Play button inside Home's Card-of-the-Day artwork surface, plus a Play button adjacent to the Decks pills (outside their tablist). Other games and Android native APK do not receive these new entries.
+- Both buttons use existing `data-act="go" data-to="#play"` navigation. No new route, implicit active-deck selection, account access, collection write, save, scanner modification, or multiplayer action is introduced. Existing Play selections remain owned by `playSetup`; the Decks shelf has no existing selected-deck handoff to extend.
+- Spacious touch **Chrome candidates** require reported touch input and **both layout-viewport dimensions >=600 CSS pixels**. This admits common 674×842 / 690×829 inner-screen layouts and 768×1024 / 1024×768 tablet layouts, while rejecting narrow covers, phone landscape, and undersized split-screen windows. The browser does **not** reliably identify physical fold state; no hinge or fold-state inference is made.
+- Current desktop UA + fine-pointer + hover admission stays intact. Mobile native/unknown capability, missing dimensions, Safari/other unverified touch browsers remain guarded. The minimum is a conservative candidate policy, not physical-device or engine certification.
+- Narrow mobile entries open the same route with a readable explanation and Home/Decks recovery links. A resize rechecks admission but never starts/closes a live match, pregame, or account-opening flow. Closing a match after the viewport became too small restores the guard. Daily artwork refresh preserves the Play node and focused control.
+- The existing `PLAY_MATCH_RELEASE_READY` value and all engine/deck/card admission are untouched. This overlay must not be used as evidence that those gates passed. Shared Community Showcase / Play online is deliberately not added.
+
+## Files to integrate
+
+Application: `desktop-play.js`, `app.js`, `tcg.js`, `views.js`, `play-menu.css`.
+
+Tests: `test-play-device-entry.mjs`, `test-play-entry-dom.mjs`, `experiments/play-entry/entry-browser.mjs`.
+
+Merge the small `app.js` hunks rather than overwriting engine-integration work. The `closePlayerMat` hunk only refreshes the route guard after existing cleanup. No engine files, package/version, service worker or deployment workflow changed.
+
+## Verification
+
+Local isolated merged fixture: `../wide-screen-entry-fixture` (a copy of the supplied source plus this overlay; the original source is unchanged).
+
+```sh
+node --test test-play-device-entry.mjs
+CARDSTASHY_DOM_MODULE=file:///tmp/forge-proof-test-tools/node_modules/happy-dom/lib/index.js \
+  node --test test-play-entry-dom.mjs
+node --test test-play-menu.mjs test-play-quick-start.mjs test-play-deck-sources.mjs \
+  test-play-artwork-views.mjs test-play-turn-controls.mjs \
+  test-play-catalog-review.mjs test-play-release-contracts.mjs
+```
+
+Passed: **8 predicate/route tests**, **7 Happy DOM tests**, **45 focused existing Play tests**; changed JS syntax checks pass. Happy DOM 21.0.4 was already installed as isolated test tooling; no application dependency changed. The DOM test can resolve `happy-dom` normally when installed, or use the shown ESM path override.
+
+All **53 available pre-existing Play tests** were also run against both original and candidate: **51 pass / 2 fail identically**. The two pre-existing `test-play-journey-ui.mjs` failures require removed “tested starter match” UI. This overlay does not restore that obsolete starter path or edit those unrelated tests. This is not a clean full-suite pass. The complete package `npm test` is not represented by the partial supplied fixture.
+
+Local Chromium launch was blocked before rendering: with a writable user-data-dir it exits 134 with `socket() failed: Operation not permitted`. No browser layout pass, device screenshot or physical foldable certification is claimed.
+
+## Required browser follow-through
+
+On CI with Playwright + Chromium and the full repository CSS/assets:
+
+```sh
+node experiments/play-entry/entry-browser.mjs
+# Optional: CARDSTASHY_PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=<ESM path>
+# Optional: CARDSTASHY_CHROMIUM_PATH=<installed browser executable>
+# Optional: CARDSTASHY_ENTRY_REPORT_DIR=<output directory>
+```
+
+This prepared (syntax-checked, **not executed**) runner exercises desktop, narrow cover, portrait/landscape inner-size, tablet, and phone-landscape viewports. It checks discoverability, 44px touch targets, horizontal overflow, shared route/guard, Back/Forward and resize restoration with a retained synthetic setup selection. It writes labeled synthetic-fixture Home/Decks/setup screenshots and a report under `test-results/play-entry`; the artwork is a synthetic gradient, not user-supplied artwork. It uses actual markup/CSS, not a real account or engine.
+
+Before release, visually inspect the real Home artwork + Decks pills in both themes, test real touch/pointer and browser zoom/address bars, fold/unfold with a live native-engine game, and run the existing engine release gates. These tests must not be described as APK, regular narrow-phone gameplay, or full physical-fold detection support.
